From 102cf5d038e24850ade57d3832729f014f724965 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MiaAI-Lab <mia.ailab1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:02:03 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 64/66] glm cuda: TF_GLM_W8A8=1 (or 32), packed 8-bit prompt
 linears on int8 activations (opt-in)

glm_mm's packed 8-bit prompt kernel unpacks int8 codes to bf16 and multiplies bf16 activations (W8A16). With
TF_GLM_W8A8=1 a prompt call (one = true, 8-bit codes, rows and K inside the scratch) instead:

- glm_q8_rows rounds the bf16 rows to int8 with an fp32 scale per row and 64 inputs (TF_GLM_W8A8=32: per 32),
  q = rint(x * 127 / max|x|), writing each 64-group permuted into the m16n8k32 B-fragment lane order of the codes as
  glm_mm already tiles them (a group's dot product does not depend on its terms' order), so the weights stay as they
  are: no copy, no re-tiling;
- glm_mm8a8 runs int8 x int8 IMMA (m16n8k32) on those rows and the tiled codes (sign-flipped from their +128 storage),
  exact int32 sums per group (or per 32-input step), each scaled by its row's and column's scales into fp32;
  row blocks fastest, 128 columns a block for a whole pass and 64 for pieces.

The scratch holds one 2048-row pass at K <= 8192 (int8 rows and [K / group][rows] scales, ~16.5 MiB a rank); other
calls keep the bf16-row kernels. TF_GLM_W8A8_SKIP_K=1024,6144,8192 (diagnostic) keeps those K widths on bf16 rows.

Measured on one RTX PRO 6000 (GLM-5.3-Flash TP2 shapes): 2048 x 12576 x 4096 1.114 -> 0.677 ms including the
quantization (1.65x), 2048 x 4096 x 8192 0.737 -> 0.442 ms, 768-row pieces 1.47x. The kernel matches its own float64
reference at bf16 output and its bytes and scales match a CPU re-implementation exactly; the activations' rounding
changes the numbers, so the flag is off by default.

The mm policy host test gains the packed_prompt field (0009's) and a W8A8 dispatch case.

